nct ZIP method ids, compact: `[0,8]` (names also accepted) | — |\n206\tNaming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime (pe+cli).\n207\tJava broke the compound law (`jar`); bytecode VMs get `<vm>_bytecode` (`neko_bytecode` in the D19 enum).\n208\t\n209\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n210\t- **A synthetic label with no derivable spelling** (D3 .NET format ~1.5 h; D17 raw `hcfg_storage`, ~10.9k POSTs over 3.5 h,\n211\t  solved only by the organizers' contract revision): stop after ~10 single-id probes plus one `hctf labels` run, write HELP.md,\n212\t  then RE-PULL THE CONTRACT periodically and diff each id's question/answer_format. Never mass-probe an exact_text label.\n213\t- **Reversing what the question already specifies** (D19): the questions gave offsets, transform and hash check; guessing from\n214\t  bytes produced a spurious partial HCFG. Read the longest question of each new family FIRST. Size fields = the exact header\n215\t  field the layout names (D20 `hcfg_resource_size` = u32 @+8, not overlay/JSON length).\n216\t- **Absence vs hidden**: `none`/`[]`/`false` is right when the thing is ABSENT (stripped d01, a re-asked field inherits it),\n217\t  wrong when it is merely HIDDEN (D19 config: packed; the race harness's `none` placeholders were rejected).\n218\t- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which one (D2). Submit unconfirmed/new fields\n219\t  ALONE; batch the bytes-derived ones. Old groups carry over by sha256: POST the known ids first (they bank as `accepted`).\n220\t- **Support members** (D3, D22): answer only from the PRIMARY assembly/classfile, but hash every member in archive order; skip\n221\t  a 5.7 MB framework DLL in brute passes.\n222\t- **\"The theme is never asked\" is NOT a rule** (D26): after 5 unasked days the crash theme was asked via a JSON sidecar inside\n223\t  the jar; the carried-over solver had no field for it (+31 s for a worker). On