{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XoHMgQQtn4vAb1MTvEJdTN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n2\t\n3\tScope: what a D28+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\n4\tare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D27), `challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/` (carried over unchanged since D23),\n5\t`challenges/day26/binary-crash-course/solver/` (same cumulative solver + a crash-sidecar branch), `challenges/day27/binary-compiler-says-what/solver/` (same solver, zero new code), `lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n6\t`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n7\t\n8\tProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\n9\tlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\n10\tD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\n11\tmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n12\t(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\n13\tappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\n14\tHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n15\t(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\n16\tno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n17\t**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n18\t`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\n19\tscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\n20\tRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\n21\tMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\n22\tprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n23\t**D21 \"Shared Custody\" (shared-library-boundaries)** = a LOADER + PLUGIN pair: `-loader.elf` (780 KB OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE,\n24\tdebug_info, NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, Dynlink `caml_natdynlink_open`/`caml_dlopen`; NO HCFG) + `-plugin.cmxs` (9 KB ET_DYN OCaml\n25\tnatdynlink plugin, exports `caml_plugin_header`/`caml_globals`/`camlPlugin_000*`, `Caml2007D002` dynheader, HCFG RAW in `.data`).\n26\t252 ids = 240 + 12: `loader_machine`/`plugin_machine` (integer 62) + config_* twice (unqualified ids name the plugin IN THE\n27\tQUESTION, plus `plugin_config_*`). The theme (exports/imports/handshake) was NOT asked. Only a routing change (question-named\n28\tmember, applied after the qualifier peel) -> CORRECT T+1:33, 0 wrong; TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s first try.\n29\t**D22 \"Bridge Troll\" (managed-native-bridge)** = an F# .NET 8 group of 3: `d22--sample.dll` (18.8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY, BSJB\n30\t`v4.0.30319`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (same bytes as d03's) + `FSharp.Core.dll` (5.7 MB stock dependency, constant sha256\n31\tacross sets). Bridge = 2 P/Invoke ImplMap rows (`getpid`@ModuleRef `libc`, `GetCurrentProcessId`@`kernel32.dll`, Winapi), trace\n32\t`fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`. HCFG RAW in `.text` (F# array blob) + an identical copy as a PE overlay; question: \"first\n33\trecord that validates\". 264 ids = 252 + 12 (3 sha256 + the d03 field family verbatim); theme NOT asked. All members silently\n34\trenamed `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`. Carried-over solver -> CORRECT T+47 s, 0 wrong; TT 12.3 s / Mastery (6 sets,\n35\t1584 ids) 18.2 s first try. FIRST day re-using an old RUNTIME with a new language (.NET: C# D3 -> F# D22).\n36\t**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n37\t.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n38\t`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n39\t`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n40\t`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n41\t`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\n42\ta PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\n43\tsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\n44\tvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\n45\tfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\n46\t**D24 \"Spot the Difference\" (patch-diffing)** = a Scala 2.13 TWIN pair: `d24--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n47\t`d24--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~4 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`, classes\n48\t`Day24<Role>000.class` (static forwarder, Main-Class) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` (module: `MODULE$`, base64 HCFG `ldc` in\n49\t`<clinit>`, `decodeConfig`, `score(String)I`, `main`), `ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig`, scala-library not bundled. Prompt: \"Two\n50\tbuilds, one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin and pinpoint exactly what changed -- then prove the old\n51\tone was really broken.\" The fix (UNASKED): only `score` changed -- vulnerable `if (s.nonEmpty) s.charAt(0) else -1` NPEs on\n52\t`null` (CWE-476); corrected `Option(s).filter(_.nonEmpty).map(_.charAt(0)).getOrElse(-1)` (+3 invokedynamic lambdas). `main`\n53\tidentical (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL lookupswitch -> decoy/success/failure), trace `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and_\n54\treversion_only` + `control_positive`. 288 ids = 276 + 12: 2 sha256, `vulnerable_format`/`corrected_format` (`jar`), 4\n55\tUNQUALIFIED config_* (\"decode both role members, require byte-for-byte equal config, use the common value\"), 4\n56\t`corrected_config_*`. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+35 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.0 s / Mastery 8 sets (2304 ids) 8.4 s\n57\tfirst try. The whole contract was reworded into specs (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order (1-based)\", HCFG layout + JAR carrier\n58\trule \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 chars\"); timed modes re-shaped domain/mutex/url too (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN...`,\n59\t`Global\\Huntress<12HEX>`, `/<word>/<10hex>`).\n60\t**D25 \"Out of Bounds\" (synthetic-vulnerability-root-cause)** = a CLOJURE AOT twin pair: `d25--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n61\t`d25--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~8.3 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Clojure factory`, Main-Class\n62\t`day25.<role>000` (gen-class stub), `<role>000__init.class` (ns loader: Vars `encoded-config` = base64 HCFG `ldc`, `parse-frame`,\n63\t`-main`), `<role>000$parse_frame.class` / `$_main.class` (AFunction/RestFn `invokeStatic`), gensym `fn__269`,\n64\t`loading__6812__auto____267`; clojure.jar not bundled. Prompt: \"Somewhere in here, the code reaches where it shouldn't. Prove the\n65\tbounds error is real, trace its reachability, and compare against the corrected twin that learned its limits.\" The bug (UNASKED):\n66\tvulnerable `parse-frame` = `(nth frame 4)` (`RT.nth(Object,int)`, no bound -> IndexOutOfBoundsException, CWE-125/129); corrected\n67\t`(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`. Reachability: `-main` gates on `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (workstation) and\n68\t`HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT == \"1\"` -> short frame `[1 2]` vs `[1 2 3 4 5]`; trace `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`/\n69\t`bounded_synthetic_fault_only`. 300 ids = 288 + 12 with the D24 id shape and wording verbatim. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code\n70\t-> CORRECT T+80 s (download ~69 s), 0 wrong; TT 10.5 s first try; **Mastery 9 sets (2700 ids): first POST INCORRECT, 55 ids in\n71\t5 sets answered with ANOTHER group's member facts (solver caches keyed on `id(bytes)` -> address reuse after GC)**; per-set\n72\tfeedback + localize + a live worker -> CORRECT ~2 min after start.\n73\t**D26 \"Crash Course\" (crash-triage)** = ONE Groovy 4 jar `d26--sample.jar` (4.5 KB, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic\n74\tGroovy factory`, Main-Class `Day26Variant000` implements `GroovyObject`: static `stageOne`->`stageTwo`->`stageThree`, stageThree\n75\t`new IllegalStateException`+`athrow`, `main` gates on `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`/`HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` via\n76\t`ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual`, HCFG base64 in `static final String encodedConfig`; + closure `Day26Variant000$_main_closure1`)\n77\tcarrying a NON-CLASS entry `crash/trace.json` = `{\"schema\":\"huntress.synthetic_crash.v1\",\"kind\":\"IllegalStateException\",\n78\t\"frames\":[\"stageThree\",\"stageTwo\",\"stageOne\"]}`; trace template family `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace`/`bounded_caught_exception_\n79\tonly` + `fault_kind`/`fault_method`. Prompt: \"It crashed ... the dump is a confession. Unwind the stack, find the faulting\n80\tinstruction, and triage what went wrong from the wreckage.\" 312 ids = 300 + 12: the d06/d07 jar family + `method_count` (10 =\n81\tevery method_info of the Main-Class incl. Groovy synthetics; the d07 \"Day 26 ... primary classfile named by that unit\" leak\n82\tresolved = the Main-Class) + the THEME, ASKED for the first time since D20: `crash_fault_method` (frames[0] verbatim) and\n83\t`crash_frames_match_methods` (every frame in the primary class method-name set -> `true`). Race solver banked 310 ids by T+45 s\n84\twith no new code; a worker added the sidecar branch (~15 lines) -> CORRECT T+76 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.3 s / Mastery 10 sets (3120 ids)\n85\t8.2 s first try. Crash values identical in all 12 deliveries (only config re-rolled).\n86\t**D27 \"Compiler Says What\" (compiler-attribution)** = a V-language TWIN pair named by COMPILER: `d27--sample-gcc.elf` (member 1,\n87\t108 KB: gcc 12.2.1 20220924 Alpine, `-Os -std=c99 -ffreestanding ... -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections`, LTO -> `.lto_priv.N`/\n88\t`.constprop.N`/`.isra.N` suffixes, ~200 symbols, DWARF 5 with DW_AT_producer, FILE `crtstuff.c`, `.eh_frame_hdr` + `.gnu.hash`) +\n89\t`d27--sample-tcc.elf` (member 2, 462 KB: tcc, STABS `.stab`/`.stabstr` instead of DWARF, `.hash` only, input sections left\n90\tunmerged (`.text._start_c`, `.rodata.str1.1`, `.data.ro`, `.data.rel.ro.local`), 4 separate NT_GNU_PROPERTY notes, ~1900 symbols\n91\tincl. `main__main`, `_vinit`, `tcc_backtrace`/`tcc_state`). Both ELF64 x86-64 ET_EXEC, dynamic musl (`/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1`,\n92\tNEEDED `libc.musl-x86_64.so.1`), Boehm GC bundled, NO `.comment`, NO build-id. HCFG RAW appended exactly at e_shoff+e_shnum*64\n93\t(379-B tail, no overlay magic) in both; question \"Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the\n94\tfirst CRC32-valid\". Trace family `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`/`equivalent_behavior_only`. Prompt: \"Every compiler signs\n95\tits work. Compare the runtime and linker fingerprints across builds and name the toolchain -- attribute this binary to its maker.\"\n96\t324 ids = 312 + 12 with the D24/D25 twin template (roles `gcc`/`tcc`: 2 sha256, `<role>_format` `elf`, `<role>_machine` integer\n97\t62, 4 consensus config_*, 2 `gcc_config_*`). Theme UNASKED. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+56 s, 0 wrong; TT\n98\t5.4 s / Mastery 11 sets (3564 ids) 14.5 s first try.\n99\tArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\n100\tmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates -> PATCH DIFFING (D24, null deref) -> BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE + REACHABILITY\n101\t(D25, OOB read) -> CRASH TRIAGE (D26, synthetic stack trace sidecar + frames-vs-methods predicate, ASKED) -> COMPILER\n102\tATTRIBUTION (D27, same source via gcc and tcc, \"runtime and linker fingerprints\", UNASKED). The vuln arc stopped after 3 days\n103\t(no native crash artifact came); D27 opened a PROVENANCE / ATTRIBUTION direction. D28-D31 (4 days left) most plausible, in\n104\torder: (1) the attribution theme deepened or ASKED (per-build compiler/version/linker/libc/debug-format/opt-level fields; a third\n105\tbackend: clang, zig cc, MSVC vs MinGW PE via Rich header; cross-compiler function matching), (2) code-similarity / family\n106\tattribution (\"which build/family is this\": fuzzy hashes, imphash, function-hash overlap, YARA), (3) a native crash/exploit sequel\n107\tof D24-D26 (core/minidump/ASan, exploitability, mitigations), (4) a capstone/backfill re-asking themes on old groups (D31).\n108\tLanguage track: D22-D26 \"new language on an old runtime\" 5x; D27 = a TRANSPILE-TO-C language (V, built by two C compilers) --\n109\tnext candidates in that family: Vala/Genie (GObject), Cython, Nim-via-clang, hxcpp, Chicken Scheme, Odin/Hare (own backends);\n110\tplus Haxe->Neko (`neko_bytecode` still unseen), Elixir/BEAM, niche JVM.\n111\t**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D27). The d07 \"Day 26 ... primary classfile named\n112\tby that unit\" leak came true (the Groovy Main-Class). No new magic token / day number in the D20-D27 contracts: next twist\n113\tunannounced.\n114\tLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n115\t`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\n116\ttokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\n117\tfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull; (g) D21: the\n118\tQUESTION can name the member for an unqualified id (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member\") -- route on the text after the id peel;\n119\t(h) D22: a group shaped like an old group inherits that group's field family; extra `.dll`s are \"delivery support only\" -- pick\n120\tthe PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics;\n121\t(i) D23: a behaviour theme (anti-analysis) on a must-not-run binary was still answered statically (header + HCFG); timed modes\n122\tre-shaped VALUES (`BRNN-<8hex>`) -- copy values verbatim, never validate their shape; (j) D24: a twin pair adds `<role>_`\n123\tqualifiers BEFORE the field family plus unqualified ids defined as the CONSENSUS of both members (decode all, assert equal);\n124\tScala logic lives in the `$` module class, not the Main-Class forwarder; (k) D25: the twin template repeated verbatim on a new\n125\tlanguage -- and the only failure was SOLVER PLUMBING at 9 Mastery sets (caches keyed on object identity): key per-member state\n126\ton (delivery, member name)/sha256, and treat \"wrong value that is a valid answer for another group\" as a routing/cache bug;\n127\t(l) D26: the theme CAN be asked, through a small JSON sidecar inside the member (`crash/trace.json`) + a structural cross-check\n128\t(frames vs method_info names) -- list every non-code entry/section/resource of a new member and parse JSON sidecars up front;\n129\t(m) D27: role tokens can be COMPILER names (`gcc`/`tcc`) -- the generic longest-member-token peel handled them; the HCFG scan\n130\tDIRECTION is in the question (\"scan backward from the end\") -- honour it per id; theme facts (producer, debug format, linker\n131\tsection layout, libc) were unasked but are recorded in Recognition cues.\n132\tAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\n133\tsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\n134\thas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\n135\thcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\n136\thcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer), `<role>_format` + `<role>_config_*` (D24 vulnerable/corrected; D27 `<role>_machine` + `<role>_format` + `gcc_config_*`, roles gcc/tcc), `crash_fault_method`, `crash_frames_match_methods` (D26).\n137\tRemaining risks: (000000) the D27 attribution theme ASKED (`<role>_compiler`/`toolchain`/`compiler_version`/`linker`/`libc`/\n138\t`debug_format`/`producer`/`opt_level` per build, or \"which member was built by X\") -- label spelling unknown (expect an enum like\n139\tD17; lowercase tool names gcc/tcc/clang), facts must come from producer/sections/symbols because `.comment` was stripped; (00000) a NATIVE crash artifact (core/minidump/sanitizer log) next to an ELF/PE: signal/exception code, faulting\n140\tRIP -> function + instruction, frame list by unwinding, fault-address class -- or the D26 sidecar idea in another container\n141\t(ELF section/PE resource/separate member) with frames as `Class.method(File:line)` or addresses; (0000) the twin arc's facts asked as fields on d24/d25 (changed function, bug class/CWE, trigger input, gating\n142\tenv vars + values, exception class, guard constant) or a NATIVE twin whose diff needs function matching; (000) the D24 diff asked as fields (changed method name/descriptor, bug class / CWE, trigger input, outcome\n143\tper build) or a NATIVE twin pair whose diff must be found by function matching (stripped?) -- see the patch-diff gaps; (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\n144\thost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\n145\tflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22 (ImplMap module/import names, callconv, marshaled types, call sites) or\n146\tan FFI bridge on another runtime (JNI, ctypes, N-API) with a native member; (1) the structure arc continues (linking internals:\n147\trelocations/GOT/PLT, symbol versions, RPATH/RUNPATH, TLS/IFUNC, or a PE DLL loader/plugin pair) with 2+ role members -- route by question text; (2) a backfill of the D18-D21 themes\n148\t(call graph, PK19/RS20 header fields, NEEDED/exports/dlopen target/plugin header); (3) Neko bytecode labels (VM machine/arch);\n149\t(4) D26 JVM classfile member; (5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D21 groups); (6) a 3+-member group (loader + several plugins,\n150\tdecoy HCFG in the loader).\n151\t\n152\tTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\n153\tInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\n154\tllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\n155\trizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\n156\tAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\n157\tjadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n158\t7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\n159\tlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\n160\tMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\n161\tunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n162\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3143ffa-b54e-4515-b64d-c18bd2fa9f3a","uuid":"071514c6-6434-40d8-9972-c60325ea11ec","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:10:00.103Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/binary-reverse-engineering.md","content":"# Coverage atlas -- binary-reverse-engineering (as of D27 post-run, 2026-10-27)\n\nScope: what a D28+ `evidence.zip` group (or backfilled old-group id) could be, how we would recognise it, which standard tool answers it, and how ready we\nare. Grounded in `reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` (lane log D1-D27), `challenges/day25/binary-out-of-bounds/solver/` (carried over unchanged since D23),\n`challenges/day26/binary-crash-course/solver/` (same cumulative solver + a crash-sidecar branch), `challenges/day27/binary-compiler-says-what/solver/` (same solver, zero new code), `lib/binary.py` (`hcfg_scan`/`hcfg_find`, `packer_info`, `unpack_upx`, `go_buildinfo`, `go_pclntab_funcs`, `rustfilt`, `macho_facts`,\n`recover_return_constants`, `ghidra_decompile`, `jar_app_classes`, `wasm_layout`) and `tests/data/binary_fixtures/TARGETS.json` (all 9 targets have fixtures).\n\nProgression so far: D1-D14 = one new compiled language per day (container nearly always ELF64 x86-64, HCFG blob re-stored per\nlanguage); D15-D16 = \"ONE SOURCE, TWO BUILDS\" pairs with a `<qualifier>_` id prefix (`stripped`/`symbolized`, `compact`/`direct`);\nD17 Ada ELF + BACKFILL #2 (160 -> 204 ids: old days' single-solve facts re-asked on their groups + the `hcfg_storage` enum after a\nmid-day contract revision); D18 Fortran ELF (theme \"call graph / no injection\" unasked, CORRECT T+11 s). **D19 \"Jack in the Box\"\n(static-unpacking)** = ONE GnuCOBOL ELF (11 KB, `libcob.so.1`, stripped) whose HCFG is NOT in the image: a `PK19` overlay is\nappended after the section-header table (`PK19|ver|k1|k2|pad|u32le len|sha256[32]|packed`, unpack `ror8(b^k2,3)^k1`, sha256-check,\nHCFG at out[0]). FIRST day whose prompt theme WAS asked on its own group: config_* only after unpacking + NEW `overlay_offset`\n(offset of the last magic) / `overlay_size` (file length - offset). The question text spelled the whole stub; 228 ids = 216 + 12,\nno backfill; CORRECT T+2:25, TT 4 s / Mastery (5 sets) 10 s first try; overlay 10808/424 constant across variants.\n**D20 \"Resourceful\" (resources-and-overlays)** = ONE Haskell ELF (GHC 9.12.2, 1.2 MB, dynamic libgmp, not stripped) + a 463-B\n`RS20` overlay at e_shoff+e_shnum*64: `RS20|ver@4|u32le res_len@8|u16le scratch_len@12|sha256(scratch)@16|HCFG resource@48 (RAW)|\nscratch` (\"private-scratch:<campaign>:inert-only\"). 240 ids = 228 + 12; NEW `hcfg_resource_size` (= u32le @8, 380). The prebuilt\nRS20/question-spec unpacker + raw HCFG scan banked 239 ids at T+27 s; one field branch -> CORRECT T+49 s, 0 wrong; TT 4.8 s /\nMastery 9.3 s first try; overlay constant across variants. D19-D20 = a \"hidden storage\" arc (packed overlay -> resource overlay;\nprompt: \"resources, overlays, bytes past the end of the sections ... map every boundary\").\n**D21 \"Shared Custody\" (shared-library-boundaries)** = a LOADER + PLUGIN pair: `-loader.elf` (780 KB OCaml 4.02.3 native PIE,\ndebug_info, NEEDED libm/libdl/libc, Dynlink `caml_natdynlink_open`/`caml_dlopen`; NO HCFG) + `-plugin.cmxs` (9 KB ET_DYN OCaml\nnatdynlink plugin, exports `caml_plugin_header`/`caml_globals`/`camlPlugin_000*`, `Caml2007D002` dynheader, HCFG RAW in `.data`).\n252 ids = 240 + 12: `loader_machine`/`plugin_machine` (integer 62) + config_* twice (unqualified ids name the plugin IN THE\nQUESTION, plus `plugin_config_*`). The theme (exports/imports/handshake) was NOT asked. Only a routing change (question-named\nmember, applied after the qualifier peel) -> CORRECT T+1:33, 0 wrong; TT 4.2 s / Mastery 9.9 s first try.\n**D22 \"Bridge Troll\" (managed-native-bridge)** = an F# .NET 8 group of 3: `d22--sample.dll` (18.8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY, BSJB\n`v4.0.30319`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (same bytes as d03's) + `FSharp.Core.dll` (5.7 MB stock dependency, constant sha256\nacross sets). Bridge = 2 P/Invoke ImplMap rows (`getpid`@ModuleRef `libc`, `GetCurrentProcessId`@`kernel32.dll`, Winapi), trace\n`fsharp_managed_native_bridge_trace`. HCFG RAW in `.text` (F# array blob) + an identical copy as a PE overlay; question: \"first\nrecord that validates\". 264 ids = 252 + 12 (3 sha256 + the d03 field family verbatim); theme NOT asked. All members silently\nrenamed `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`. Carried-over solver -> CORRECT T+47 s, 0 wrong; TT 12.3 s / Mastery (6 sets,\n1584 ids) 18.2 s first try. FIRST day re-using an old RUNTIME with a new language (.NET: C# D3 -> F# D22).\n**D23 \"Trust Issues\" (anti-analysis-recognition)** = a VB.NET .NET 8 group of 2: `d23--sample.dll` (8 KB, PE32 i386 ILONLY,\n.text/.rsrc/.reloc, BSJB `v4.0.30319`, AssemblyRefs System.Runtime/Microsoft.VisualBasic.Core/System.Text.Json/System.Console,\n`StandardModuleAttribute`, `VB$AnonymousType_0`8`) + `sample.runtimeconfig.json` (d03's bytes). Predicates (theme, UNASKED):\n`Debugger.get_IsAttached`, `Stopwatch.StartNew`/`get_ElapsedTicks` (clock), `Environment.get_ProcessorCount`,\n`GetEnvironmentVariable(\"HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\")` vs workstation/analysis/sandbox -> branch success/decoy/failure, trace\n`vbnet_anti_analysis_predicate_trace`/`inert_predicate_only`, field `analysis_detected`. No ImplMap, no FieldRVA. HCFG RAW ONCE as\na PE overlay right after `.reloc` (7680 = EOF-380). 276 ids = 264 + 12 (2 sha256 + d22 family + `xor_key_hex`). Carried-over\nsolver -> CORRECT T+84 s (22 s download), 0 wrong; TT 13.0 s / Mastery 7 sets (1932 ids) 7.9 s first try. NEW in timed modes:\nvalue SHAPES re-rolled (`BR23-<8 uppercase hex>` campaign, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, d01 FILE symbol `sample.c`) -- harmless\nfor a verbatim-copying solver. THIRD .NET language (C# D3, F# D22, VB.NET D23) and the first BEHAVIOUR (evasion) theme.\n**D24 \"Spot the Difference\" (patch-diffing)** = a Scala 2.13 TWIN pair: `d24--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n`d24--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~4 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Scala factory`, classes\n`Day24<Role>000.class` (static forwarder, Main-Class) + `Day24<Role>000$.class` (module: `MODULE$`, base64 HCFG `ldc` in\n`<clinit>`, `decodeConfig`, `score(String)I`, `main`), `ScalaSignature`/`ScalaSig`, scala-library not bundled. Prompt: \"Two\nbuilds, one fix. Diff the vulnerable function against its corrected twin and pinpoint exactly what changed -- then prove the old\none was really broken.\" The fix (UNASKED): only `score` changed -- vulnerable `if (s.nonEmpty) s.charAt(0) else -1` NPEs on\n`null` (CWE-476); corrected `Option(s).filter(_.nonEmpty).map(_.charAt(0)).getOrElse(-1)` (+3 invokedynamic lambdas). `main`\nidentical (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL lookupswitch -> decoy/success/failure), trace `scala_patch_diff_trace`/`benign_control_and_\nreversion_only` + `control_positive`. 288 ids = 276 + 12: 2 sha256, `vulnerable_format`/`corrected_format` (`jar`), 4\nUNQUALIFIED config_* (\"decode both role members, require byte-for-byte equal config, use the common value\"), 4\n`corrected_config_*`. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+35 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.0 s / Mastery 8 sets (2304 ids) 8.4 s\nfirst try. The whole contract was reworded into specs (sha256 \"ZIP central-directory order (1-based)\", HCFG layout + JAR carrier\nrule \"Base64-alphabet UTF-8 constants >= 80 chars\"); timed modes re-shaped domain/mutex/url too (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN...`,\n`Global\\Huntress<12HEX>`, `/<word>/<10hex>`).\n**D25 \"Out of Bounds\" (synthetic-vulnerability-root-cause)** = a CLOJURE AOT twin pair: `d25--sample-vulnerable.jar` (member 1) +\n`d25--sample-corrected.jar` (member 2), ~8.3 KB each, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic Clojure factory`, Main-Class\n`day25.<role>000` (gen-class stub), `<role>000__init.class` (ns loader: Vars `encoded-config` = base64 HCFG `ldc`, `parse-frame`,\n`-main`), `<role>000$parse_frame.class` / `$_main.class` (AFunction/RestFn `invokeStatic`), gensym `fn__269`,\n`loading__6812__auto____267`; clojure.jar not bundled. Prompt: \"Somewhere in here, the code reaches where it shouldn't. Prove the\nbounds error is real, trace its reachability, and compare against the corrected twin that learned its limits.\" The bug (UNASKED):\nvulnerable `parse-frame` = `(nth frame 4)` (`RT.nth(Object,int)`, no bound -> IndexOutOfBoundsException, CWE-125/129); corrected\n`(if (< 4 (count frame)) (nth frame 4) -1)`. Reachability: `-main` gates on `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL` (workstation) and\n`HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT == \"1\"` -> short frame `[1 2]` vs `[1 2 3 4 5]`; trace `clojure_bounds_root_cause_trace`/\n`bounded_synthetic_fault_only`. 300 ids = 288 + 12 with the D24 id shape and wording verbatim. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code\n-> CORRECT T+80 s (download ~69 s), 0 wrong; TT 10.5 s first try; **Mastery 9 sets (2700 ids): first POST INCORRECT, 55 ids in\n5 sets answered with ANOTHER group's member facts (solver caches keyed on `id(bytes)` -> address reuse after GC)**; per-set\nfeedback + localize + a live worker -> CORRECT ~2 min after start.\n**D26 \"Crash Course\" (crash-triage)** = ONE Groovy 4 jar `d26--sample.jar` (4.5 KB, manifest `Created-By: Huntress deterministic\nGroovy factory`, Main-Class `Day26Variant000` implements `GroovyObject`: static `stageOne`->`stageTwo`->`stageThree`, stageThree\n`new IllegalStateException`+`athrow`, `main` gates on `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`/`HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT` via\n`ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual`, HCFG base64 in `static final String encodedConfig`; + closure `Day26Variant000$_main_closure1`)\ncarrying a NON-CLASS entry `crash/trace.json` = `{\"schema\":\"huntress.synthetic_crash.v1\",\"kind\":\"IllegalStateException\",\n\"frames\":[\"stageThree\",\"stageTwo\",\"stageOne\"]}`; trace template family `groovy_synthetic_crash_trace`/`bounded_caught_exception_\nonly` + `fault_kind`/`fault_method`. Prompt: \"It crashed ... the dump is a confession. Unwind the stack, find the faulting\ninstruction, and triage what went wrong from the wreckage.\" 312 ids = 300 + 12: the d06/d07 jar family + `method_count` (10 =\nevery method_info of the Main-Class incl. Groovy synthetics; the d07 \"Day 26 ... primary classfile named by that unit\" leak\nresolved = the Main-Class) + the THEME, ASKED for the first time since D20: `crash_fault_method` (frames[0] verbatim) and\n`crash_frames_match_methods` (every frame in the primary class method-name set -> `true`). Race solver banked 310 ids by T+45 s\nwith no new code; a worker added the sidecar branch (~15 lines) -> CORRECT T+76 s, 0 wrong; TT 5.3 s / Mastery 10 sets (3120 ids)\n8.2 s first try. Crash values identical in all 12 deliveries (only config re-rolled).\n**D27 \"Compiler Says What\" (compiler-attribution)** = a V-language TWIN pair named by COMPILER: `d27--sample-gcc.elf` (member 1,\n108 KB: gcc 12.2.1 20220924 Alpine, `-Os -std=c99 -ffreestanding ... -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections`, LTO -> `.lto_priv.N`/\n`.constprop.N`/`.isra.N` suffixes, ~200 symbols, DWARF 5 with DW_AT_producer, FILE `crtstuff.c`, `.eh_frame_hdr` + `.gnu.hash`) +\n`d27--sample-tcc.elf` (member 2, 462 KB: tcc, STABS `.stab`/`.stabstr` instead of DWARF, `.hash` only, input sections left\nunmerged (`.text._start_c`, `.rodata.str1.1`, `.data.ro`, `.data.rel.ro.local`), 4 separate NT_GNU_PROPERTY notes, ~1900 symbols\nincl. `main__main`, `_vinit`, `tcc_backtrace`/`tcc_state`). Both ELF64 x86-64 ET_EXEC, dynamic musl (`/lib/ld-musl-x86_64.so.1`,\nNEEDED `libc.musl-x86_64.so.1`), Boehm GC bundled, NO `.comment`, NO build-id. HCFG RAW appended exactly at e_shoff+e_shnum*64\n(379-B tail, no overlay magic) in both; question \"Scan backward from the end of the member for literal HCFG magic and accept the\nfirst CRC32-valid\". Trace family `v_cross_backend_attribution_trace`/`equivalent_behavior_only`. Prompt: \"Every compiler signs\nits work. Compare the runtime and linker fingerprints across builds and name the toolchain -- attribute this binary to its maker.\"\n324 ids = 312 + 12 with the D24/D25 twin template (roles `gcc`/`tcc`: 2 sha256, `<role>_format` `elf`, `<role>_machine` integer\n62, 4 consensus config_*, 2 `gcc_config_*`). Theme UNASKED. Carried-over solver, ZERO new code -> CORRECT T+56 s, 0 wrong; TT\n5.4 s / Mastery 11 sets (3564 ids) 14.5 s first try.\nArc since D18 = one structure/behaviour concept per day: call graph -> packing -> resources/overlays -> shared libraries ->\nmanaged/native bridge -> anti-analysis predicates -> PATCH DIFFING (D24, null deref) -> BOUNDS-ERROR ROOT CAUSE + REACHABILITY\n(D25, OOB read) -> CRASH TRIAGE (D26, synthetic stack trace sidecar + frames-vs-methods predicate, ASKED) -> COMPILER\nATTRIBUTION (D27, same source via gcc and tcc, \"runtime and linker fingerprints\", UNASKED). The vuln arc stopped after 3 days\n(no native crash artifact came); D27 opened a PROVENANCE / ATTRIBUTION direction. D28-D31 (4 days left) most plausible, in\norder: (1) the attribution theme deepened or ASKED (per-build compiler/version/linker/libc/debug-format/opt-level fields; a third\nbackend: clang, zig cc, MSVC vs MinGW PE via Rich header; cross-compiler function matching), (2) code-similarity / family\nattribution (\"which build/family is this\": fuzzy hashes, imphash, function-hash overlap, YARA), (3) a native crash/exploit sequel\nof D24-D26 (core/minidump/ASan, exploitability, mitigations), (4) a capstone/backfill re-asking themes on old groups (D31).\nLanguage track: D22-D26 \"new language on an old runtime\" 5x; D27 = a TRANSPILE-TO-C language (V, built by two C compilers) --\nnext candidates in that family: Vala/Genie (GObject), Cython, Nim-via-clang, hxcpp, Chicken Scheme, Odin/Hare (own backends);\nplus Haxe->Neko (`neko_bytecode` still unseen), Elixir/BEAM, niche JVM.\n**Forward hints still open**: `neko_bytecode` in the format enum (unseen through D27). The d07 \"Day 26 ... primary classfile named\nby that unit\" leak came true (the Groovy Main-Class). No new magic token / day number in the D20-D27 contracts: next twist\nunannounced.\nLessons for D21+: (a) read the longest question of each new family first -- it is the layout spec; (b) every `*_size`/`*_offset`/\n`*_sha256` id maps to ONE named header field: parse the spec into a struct and expose every field; (c) grep each contract for\ntokens/days that are not today's; (d) header ids of the new member are answered by the carried-over solver; the twist is the new\nfield family; (e) `none` only for ABSENT things; (f) unguessable labels get fixed by contract revision -- re-pull; (g) D21: the\nQUESTION can name the member for an unqualified id (\"Use the d21-- plugin.cmxs member\") -- route on the text after the id peel;\n(h) D22: a group shaped like an old group inherits that group's field family; extra `.dll`s are \"delivery support only\" -- pick\nthe PRIMARY assembly, never key on `variant-` in basenames (renamed to `sample`), and keep FIRST-valid-HCFG semantics;\n(i) D23: a behaviour theme (anti-analysis) on a must-not-run binary was still answered statically (header + HCFG); timed modes\nre-shaped VALUES (`BRNN-<8hex>`) -- copy values verbatim, never validate their shape; (j) D24: a twin pair adds `<role>_`\nqualifiers BEFORE the field family plus unqualified ids defined as the CONSENSUS of both members (decode all, assert equal);\nScala logic lives in the `$` module class, not the Main-Class forwarder; (k) D25: the twin template repeated verbatim on a new\nlanguage -- and the only failure was SOLVER PLUMBING at 9 Mastery sets (caches keyed on object identity): key per-member state\non (delivery, member name)/sha256, and treat \"wrong value that is a valid answer for another group\" as a routing/cache bug;\n(l) D26: the theme CAN be asked, through a small JSON sidecar inside the member (`crash/trace.json`) + a structural cross-check\n(frames vs method_info names) -- list every non-code entry/section/resource of a new member and parse JSON sidecars up front;\n(m) D27: role tokens can be COMPILER names (`gcc`/`tcc`) -- the generic longest-member-token peel handled them; the HCFG scan\nDIRECTION is in the question (\"scan backward from the end\") -- honour it per id; theme facts (producer, debug format, linker\nsection layout, libc) were unasked but are recorded in Recognition cues.\nAsked field names: config_*, format (enum), machine, architecture, elf_class, elf_type, endianness, entry_point, symbols,\nsection_names, disassembly, marker, recover_code, has_symtab, has_cpp_*, has_go_runtime, has_rust_mangled_symbol,\nhas_coroutine_runtime, mangled_score_symbol, typeinfo_symbol, methods, access_flags, method_count, has_hcfg_section, hcfg_offset,\nhcfg_version, hcfg_storage (enum), xor_key_hex, metadata_version, compression_methods, overlay_offset, overlay_size,\nhcfg_resource_size, `<role>_machine` (D21 loader/plugin, integer), `<role>_format` + `<role>_config_*` (D24 vulnerable/corrected; D27 `<role>_machine` + `<role>_format` + `gcc_config_*`, roles gcc/tcc), `crash_fault_method`, `crash_frames_match_methods` (D26).\nRemaining risks: (000000) the D27 attribution theme ASKED (`<role>_compiler`/`toolchain`/`compiler_version`/`linker`/`libc`/\n`debug_format`/`producer`/`opt_level` per build, or \"which member was built by X\") -- label spelling unknown (expect an enum like\nD17; lowercase tool names gcc/tcc/clang), facts must come from producer/sections/symbols because `.comment` was stripped; (00000) a NATIVE crash artifact (core/minidump/sanitizer log) next to an ELF/PE: signal/exception code, faulting\nRIP -> function + instruction, frame list by unwinding, fault-address class -- or the D26 sidecar idea in another container\n(ELF section/PE resource/separate member) with frames as `Class.method(File:line)` or addresses; (0000) the twin arc's facts asked as fields on d24/d25 (changed function, bug class/CWE, trigger input, gating\nenv vars + values, exception class, guard constant) or a NATIVE twin whose diff needs function matching; (000) the D24 diff asked as fields (changed method name/descriptor, bug class / CWE, trigger input, outcome\nper build) or a NATIVE twin pair whose diff must be found by function matching (stripped?) -- see the patch-diff gaps; (00) the D23 predicates asked as fields (predicate list, env var name, compared host-model values, branch per\nhost model, timing threshold, `analysis_detected` verdict) or an obfuscation sequel (encrypted strings/IL, anti-disassembly,\nflattened control flow) where the HCFG is only reachable through a decoder; (0) the bridge theme backfilled on d22 (ImplMap module/import names, callconv, marshaled types, call sites) or\nan FFI bridge on another runtime (JNI, ctypes, N-API) with a native member; (1) the structure arc continues (linking internals:\nrelocations/GOT/PLT, symbol versions, RPATH/RUNPATH, TLS/IFUNC, or a PE DLL loader/plugin pair) with 2+ role members -- route by question text; (2) a backfill of the D18-D21 themes\n(call graph, PK19/RS20 header fields, NEEDED/exports/dlopen target/plugin header); (3) Neko bytecode labels (VM machine/arch);\n(4) D26 JVM classfile member; (5) per-language fact backfills (D8-D21 groups); (6) a 3+-member group (loader + several plugins,\ndecoy HCFG in the loader).\n\nTool legend: **[I]** installed (`source bin/env.sh`; checked with `which`/`ls`), **[M]** missing.\nInstalled: readelf/objdump/nm/c++filt/strings/objcopy (binutils x86-64 + aarch64-linux-gnu-objdump), llvm-18 (llvm-objdump-18,\nllvm-readobj-18, llvm-otool, llvm-lipo, llvm-nm, llvm-dwarfdump, llvm-cxxfilt-18 under /usr/lib/llvm-18/bin), file, binwalk, upx 4.2.4,\nrizin 0.9.1 (`bin/rizin`, `rz-bin`, `rz-asm`, `rz-find`, `rz-diff`) + radare2/rabin2, Ghidra (`bin/analyzeHeadless`, processors incl.\nAARCH64/ARM/MIPS/PowerPC/RISCV/Sparc/x86/JVM/Dalvik), GoReSym, rustfilt, swift-demangle, nim-demangle, ilspycmd, dotnet, java/javap,\njadx, dex2jar, apktool, pyinstxtractor, pycdc/pycdas, autoit-ripper, hbc-decompiler, gdb + gdb-multiarch, ltrace/strace, yara, wabt (wasm-objdump/wasm2wat/wat2wasm/wasm-decompile), floss (.venv), luac,\n7z, xxd; venv python: capstone, unicorn, angr, lief, pyelftools, pefile, dnfile, pycryptodome, pyzipper, xdis/uncompyle6/decompyle3,\nlz4, yara. Cross compilers: aarch64-linux-gnu-gcc-15, clang-18 (no lld/wasm-ld: other targets compile to `.o` only).\nMissing: qemu-user(-static), wasm-ld/lld, wasmtime, capa, Detect-It-Easy (diec), de4dot, monodis, erlang (beam_disasm),\nunluac/luajit-decompiler (luac present), blutter, srecord (srec_cat), binutils-multiarch, checksec, python zstandard/brotli, rzpipe/r2pipe.\n","numLines":162,"startLine":1,"totalLine