{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hkkfos1p4M7oGABxTQ1q73","type":"tool_result","content":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nSTEP 1  file -b F ; xxd -l 64 F            -> container + arch + stripped/static/PIE in one line\n  7f454c46 ELF: byte4 1=ELF32 2=ELF64; byte5 1=LE 2=BE (BE => read e_machine/HCFG ints big-endian)\n  4d5a MZ->PE: Machine 0x14c i386 | 0x8664 x86-64 | 0xaa64 AArch64 | 0x1c0/0x1c4 ARM; \"Mono/.Net\" => pe_cli (C# D3, F# D22,\n    VB.NET D23: i386 ILONLY, BSJB v4.0.30319; answer from the PRIMARY .dll, FSharp.Core/System.* = support members)\n  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n    jar = `jar` for Java/Kotlin/Scala/Clojure/Groovy; HCFG ldc may sit outside the Main-Class: Scala `Foo$.class`, Clojure\n    `<ns>__init.class` (+ `<ns>$<fn>` per defn); Groovy = Main-Class (`GroovyObject`, `encodedConfig`) + `$_main_closure1`\n    ALWAYS `unzip -l`: NON-class entries carry theme data (D26 `crash/trace.json`) -- parse them before reading questions\n  4e454b4f 'NEKO' => Neko VM bytecode: format `neko_bytecode` (in the GM enum since D19; unseen)\n  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32`; lib.binary.wasm_layout / wasm-objdump -x F; HCFG RAW data seg 0\n  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\nSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|V panic|tcc_backtrace|UPX|HCFG|SENGR' -> toolchain+blob\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -p -c -constants / jadx | Swift swift-demangle | Nim\n  nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | else rizin 'aaa;afl' / Ghidra headless (no exec)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  ALWAYS check the tail: image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (PE: pefile overlay start); len > image_end => OVERLAY with a\n  day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 D20; D27 = bare RAW HCFG, no magic, \"scan backward from the end\" = rfind loop until crc-valid):\n  o = data.rfind(magic); parse EVERY header field the QUESTION lists (size ids = that field,\n  hcfg_resource_size = u32@8), verify bounds/sha256, run its transform, HCFG at the stated offset; overlay_size = len-o.\n  NOT FOUND => hidden elsewhere: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / gaps between sections (slack) /\n  custom ELF notes (`readelf -nW`) / compressed `C`-flag sections (`readelf -zx`) / archive appended after the image;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/\n  plugin, vulnerable/corrected, D27 gcc/tcc; LONGEST member-name token); THEN the member the QUESTION names; \"decode both role\n  members, require equal\" (D24/D25/D27) => decode all, assert equal, use the common value; sha256_K = zip order | config_* verbatim |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  New-language member = carried-over header ids (post first); twist = the NEW field family: its longest question is the\n  spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\nCRASH (D26, ASKED): sidecar {\"schema\":\"huntress.synthetic_crash.v1\",\"kind\":<Exception>,\"frames\":[innermost..outermost]};\n  fault method = frames[0] verbatim; \"frames match methods\" = every frame in the primary class's method_info names -> true/false.\n  Native sequel: core `readelf -nW` NT_PRSTATUS RIP / MDMP ExceptionStream -> `addr2line -f -e bin`, capstone it. Never run it.\nATTRIBUTION (D27 theme, UNASKED; roles = compiler names): gcc = DW_AT_producer `GNU C99 <ver> <flags>` (`readelf --debug-dump=\n  info F|grep -m2 producer`), `.lto_priv/.constprop/.isra` syms, FILE crtstuff.c, DWARF; tcc = `.stab`/`.stabstr`, `tcc_backtrace`,\n  `.hash` only, unmerged `.text.<x>`/`.rodata.str1.1`, 1 GNU_PROPERTY note per object; libc = PT_INTERP; `.comment` may be ABSENT.\nTHEME FACTS (unasked): dynamic_trace.v1 template (family `<lang>_<theme>_trace` names the theme), env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\n  (+TRIGGER_FAULT); D21 NEEDED/exports; D22 ImplMap; D23 predicates; D24 `score` null->NPE; D25 `parse-frame` (nth v 4)->IOOBE.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): marker, recover_code (decimal), mangled_score/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK/_ZTI; PE .text$),\n  has_* true/false, methods (JSON incl <init>), access_flags (decimal), method_count (ALL method_info). Derive from bytes.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: <=10 probes, HELP.md, re-pull contract. MASTERY: cache per (delivery, member)/sha256, never id(bytes).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each contract for tokens/days not today's (open: enum `neko_bytecode`). Values re-shaped in TT/M: copy verbatim.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"crash-sidecar-generic-parser\", \"concept\": \"Crash/trace SIDECAR anywhere in a member (D26 shape generalised): locate a crash record in a jar/zip entry, ELF section or note, PE RCDATA/.NET resource, overlay or a separate `dNN--*.json`/`.txt` member, and expose its facts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 asked crash_fault_method (= frames[0] verbatim) and crash_frames_match_methods (every frame in the primary classfile method-name set) from `crash/trace.json` = {schema: huntress.synthetic_crash.v1, kind, frames[innermost..]} inside challenges/day26/binary-crash-course/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d26--sample.jar. Build lib.binary.crash_sidecar(member_bytes) -> {schema, kind, frames, frame_count, fault_method, outer_method, raw}: search zip entries whose name ends trace.json/crash*.json/*.trace, any JSON object with a `frames`/`stack`/`backtrace` list in raw bytes (ELF section, PE resource, overlay, UTF-16 too), and text traces. Normalise frame strings in every likely shape: bare `stageThree`, `Class.method`, `pkg.Class.method(File.groovy:12)`, `module!func+0x1a`, `func+0x1a/0x40`, `#0 0x... in func file:line`, raw `0x401136` (-> resolve via symtab). Predicates: frames subset of method set (JVM method_info names, .NET MethodDef names, ELF/PE FUNC symbols), frame[0] defined in the primary unit, frames form a valid static call chain (see jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts). Missing sidecar -> `none`/`false`. Fixtures: the D26 jar + synthesised variants (renamed entry path, frames with descriptors, sidecar in an ELF section).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts\", \"concept\": \"Static call chain + throw sites for a JVM primary class (what a stack trace should look like): per method its callees and the exceptions it throws, so a reported trace can be verified or derived\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 (unasked): Day26Variant000 main -> stageOne -> stageTwo -> stageThree (invokestatic), stageThree = `new java/lang/IllegalStateException` ... `athrow`; main compares HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT via ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual and catches the exception (trace effects bounded_caught_exception_only). Build from Code attributes: callees per method (invokestatic/virtual/special/interface; invokedynamic bootstrap names; Groovy dynamic call sites = the `$createCallSiteArray_1` string array when the class is not @CompileStatic), thrown classes (`new X` ... `athrow`, `athrow` of a param), exception_table (handler ranges + catch types), LineNumberTable lines per throw, `throws` (Exceptions attribute). Answers: fault_method from bytecode alone (the only method that athrows the trace kind), call depth, caller of X, catch site, line of the throw, `frames_are_call_chain` predicate. Same for Kotlin/Scala ($ module) /Clojure (invokeStatic) layouts; fixtures: D24/D25/D26 jars.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-core-dump-triage\", \"concept\": \"Native crash dump: ELF core file (ET_CORE) as a group member beside its executable -- signal, faulting RIP, registers, mapped files, fault address\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural native sequel to D26 ('the dump is a confession ... find the faulting instruction'). Parse PT_NOTE (owner CORE/LINUX): NT_PRSTATUS (pr_cursig, pr_pid, user_regs_struct order r15..rip,cs,eflags,rsp,ss,fs_base..), NT_PRPSINFO (pr_fname, pr_psargs), NT_SIGINFO (si_signo, si_errno, si_code SEGV_MAPERR=1/ACCERR=2, si_addr), NT_AUXV (AT_ENTRY, AT_PHDR, AT_EXECFN), NT_FILE (count, page_size, start/end/file_ofs + names), NT_FPREGSET; PT_LOAD memory for stack reads. Map RIP to (module, file offset) via NT_FILE and to a function via the companion member's symtab/.eh_frame (build-id NT_GNU_BUILD_ID match). Labels: signal names `SIGSEGV`/`SIGABRT`/`SIGFPE`/`SIGILL`/`SIGBUS`/`SIGTRAP` and numbers 11/6/8/4/7/5; hex with 0x. Fixtures: compile tiny C crashers (null write, div0, abort via __stack_chk_fail, ud2) and make cores with `gdb -batch -ex run -ex generate-core-file` on OUR fixtures only (never run a challenge sample); 32-bit + AArch64 cores via synthetic note writers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"faulting-instruction-locator\", \"concept\": \"'Find the faulting instruction': map a fault pc/offset (from a core, minidump, text report or the question) to its function and decode/classify the instruction\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Inputs: VA or file offset + member. Containing function via .symtab/.dynsym FUNC ranges, then .eh_frame FDE ranges (stripped), PE .pdata RUNTIME_FUNCTION, Mach-O LC_FUNCTION_STARTS; JVM: bytecode offset -> method via Code ranges + LineNumberTable. Decode with capstone intel in the GM convention (lowercase, decimal immediates, no trailing space: `mov dword ptr [rax], 0`), plus facts: mnemonic, memory operand base/index/disp, access size, read vs write, offset within function (`func+0x1a`). Classify: null-pointer read/write (base reg 0 / si_addr < 0x1000), divide error (`div`/`idiv`, SIGFPE), `ud2`/`int3`/`hlt` trap, call through bad pointer, stack-protector abort (`call __stack_chk_fail`), assert/abort. Fixtures from the elf-core-dump-triage crashers (x86-64, i386, AArch64).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bug-reachability-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"'Trace its reachability': the call path from the entry point to the vulnerable call and the input/env predicates that must hold (env var names + compared values, argv/stdin/file checks), per member and per host model\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 (unasked): Clojure `-main` -> System.getenv(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) compared to `workstation`, getenv(HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT) Util.equiv \\\"1\\\" -> chooses frame const__3 [1 2] (2 elements) vs const__7 [1 2 3 4 5] -> parse-frame (nth 4). Build lib.binary.reachability_facts(member, target_fn): JVM -- walk invokeStatic/IFn.invoke edges from main/-main (resolve Var.getRawRoot of `RT.var` names to fn classes), collect the getenv/equals/equiv/lookupswitch predicates on the path and the constant collections (Tuple.create arity / array sizes) fed to the target; native -- capstone call graph (prebuilt callgraph-indirect-flow-facts) + getenv/strcmp/argv compares before the call. Output: call_path (JSON names), gate_env_vars (JSON, order of use), gate_values, trigger_condition text, reachable_for_<host_model> booleans, input_size_on_trigger (2) vs safe (5). Fixtures: D25 jars + D24 jars + a C twin with getenv-gated memcpy.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crash-exploitability-facts\", \"concept\": \"Native 'prove it is broken' facts: stack buffer size, distance from buffer to saved RIP/canary, overflow length that faults, faulting instruction, mitigations (canary/NX/PIE/RELRO)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"From capstone over the vulnerable function: frame size (`sub rsp, N`), buffer offset (`lea rdi, [rbp-0xNN]` passed to gets/strcpy/read/memcpy/scanf %s), canary load `mov rax, fs:0x28` + `__stack_chk_fail`, read length argument; distance_to_return = NN + 8 (rbp) ; first faulting length via unicorn emulation with a cyclic (de Bruijn) pattern; checksec-style facts from program headers (GNU_STACK flags, GNU_RELRO + BIND_NOW, ET_DYN+INTERP). Corrected twin: same facts showing the bound. Fixtures: gcc -fno-stack-protector / -fstack-protector-strong pairs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"symbolic-input-solver\", \"concept\": \"Find an input that reaches a target (vulnerable path, accept branch, decoy vs success) with angr/z3 when hand-evaluation is impractical: crackme/license checks, multi-step guards\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"angr (venv) blank_state at the function with symbolic args/stdin, avoid-list = failure branches, find = target address (crash site, success string xref, `return 1`); z3 directly for JVM/IL guard chains extracted by the bytecode evaluators (hashCode lookupswitch -> string preimage among the binary's own literals first). Hard caps: 60 s, 4 GB; output the concrete input as hex + printable. Fixtures: gcc serial-check (per-char xor/add compare), a hash-gated branch, and the D24 host-model lookupswitch (preimages analysis/workstation/sandbox). D25 'trace its reachability' = which env values reach the bug: include the D25 Clojure `-main` (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT compares) as a fixture.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"member-basename-vocabulary\", \"concept\": \"Member basenames re-labelled between days (D22: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`, `sample-stripped`, `sample-plugin`) and questions reworded to match; D23 timed modes re-shaped the VALUES too (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Group members by the `dNN--` prefix only; derive role/tag from the token after the stem (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/plugin) or from the extension; never require `variant-` or `sample`. A regression case with renamed members (sed the names in a copy of the zip listing) keeps the router honest. D23: never regex-validate a value shape (`BRNN-\\\\d{3}`) or derive anything from the `00V` index; copy decoded values verbatim. D24 timed modes re-shaped domain (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`), mutex (`Global\\\\Huntress<12 uppercase hex>`) and url (`https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`) too; role tokens `vulnerable`/`corrected` follow `sample-`. D25 timed modes added domain/url words edge/cache/vault/proxy/node and path words vault/edge/stage/sync/gate; url host word independent of the domain word.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'. D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open). D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'. D25: no new token/day; d25 ids copy the D24 wording verbatim; Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open (Clojure's `__init` vs gen-class stub is a 2nd example of 'primary classfile named by that unit'). D26: the d07 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit' leak came TRUE (Groovy jar; the primary classfile = the manifest Main-Class `Day26Variant000`, not the `$_main_closure1` closure). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open; D26 contract added no new token/day.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c3143ffa-b54e-4515-b64d-c18bd2fa9f3a","uuid":"fc1dacf5-38da-4551-ad04-03a34359b0d8","timestamp":"2026-10-28T13:10:10.684Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n```\nSTEP 1  file -b F ; xxd -l 64 F            -> container + arch + stripped/static/PIE in one line\n  7f454c46 ELF: byte4 1=ELF32 2=ELF64; byte5 1=LE 2=BE (BE => read e_machine/HCFG ints big-endian)\n  4d5a MZ->PE: Machine 0x14c i386 | 0x8664 x86-64 | 0xaa64 AArch64 | 0x1c0/0x1c4 ARM; \"Mono/.Net\" => pe_cli (C# D3, F# D22,\n    VB.NET D23: i386 ILONLY, BSJB v4.0.30319; answer from the PRIMARY .dll, FSharp.Core/System.* = support members)\n  cffaedfe/cefaedfe Mach-O thin; cafebabe + small u32 nfat => Mach-O FAT (NOT a Java class) ; format word presumed `macho`\n  504b0304 zip/jar/apk (keep nested jars whole) ; 1b4c7561 Lua ; 1b4c4a LuaJIT ; FOR1..BEAM Erlang ; 4243c0de LLVM bitcode\n    jar = `jar` for Java/Kotlin/Scala/Clojure/Groovy; HCFG ldc may sit outside the Main-Class: Scala `Foo$.class`, Clojure\n    `<ns>__init.class` (+ `<ns>$<fn>` per defn); Groovy = Main-Class (`GroovyObject`, `encodedConfig`) + `$_main_closure1`\n    ALWAYS `unzip -l`: NON-class entries carry theme data (D26 `crash/trace.json`) -- parse them before reading questions\n  4e454b4f 'NEKO' => Neko VM bytecode: format `neko_bytecode` (in the GM enum since D19; unseen)\n  0061736d \\0asm WASM (D16): format `wasm`, architecture `wasm32`; lib.binary.wasm_layout / wasm-objdump -x F; HCFG RAW data seg 0\n  ':10' text lines => Intel HEX ; 'S0'/'S1' => S-record ; no magic + ARM vector table => raw firmware (rizin -m base)\nSTEP 2  rz-bin -I F   (or readelf -hlSW F)  -> lang, machine, bits, endian, static, stripped, pic, relro, nx, canary\n  e_machine: 3 x86 | 62 x86-64 | 40 ARM | 183 AArch64 | 8 MIPS | 20 PPC | 21 PPC64 | 243 RISC-V | 2/43 SPARC\n  labels: GM-confirmed x86-64/x86/AArch64/ARM (ELF), i386/x86-64 (PE); others = readelf spelling first, then EM_ name minus\n  prefix; kind:integer => decimal e_machine. Dispatch on answer_format.kind, never on field name.\n  no .symtab => stripped (answer [] / none / false); no INTERP => static; ET_DYN+INTERP => PIE; ET_REL => object file\n  UPX0/UPX1 sections or \"UPX!\" or entropy>7.2 => PACKED: upx -t F; cp F /tmp/x; upx -d /tmp/x (fix zeroed UPX! first)\nSTEP 3  strings -a -n6 F | grep -m8 -E 'GCC:|clang|rustc|go1\\.|GHC |OCaml|caml_|FPC |Crystal|zig|GNAT Version|gfortran|DMD|Nim|\n        swift|_kDart|kfun:|__svm|MEI|nuitka|AU3!|Borland|MSVBVM|libcob|V panic|tcc_backtrace|UPX|HCFG|SENGR' -> toolchain+blob\n  toolchain -> tool: Go GoReSym | Rust rustfilt | .NET ilspycmd | jar javap -p -c -constants / jadx | Swift swift-demangle | Nim\n  nim-demangle | PyInstaller pyinstxtractor+pycdc | AutoIt autoit-ripper | else rizin 'aaa;afl' / Ghidra headless (no exec)\nHCFG (every new member since D2)\n  python: from lib.binary import hcfg_find, hcfg_scan; hcfg_find(open(F,'rb').read())  -> config, offset, encoding, key, crc_ok\n  raw magic 'HCFG' | b64 'SENGR' | hex '48434647' | rot13 'FRATE' | b64-zlib 'eJ' | b64-gzip 'H4sI' -> covered by hcfg_scan\n  accept only crc32(plain)==header crc AND JSON parses; keep scanning past decoys (D9 had two raw-magic decoys)\n  ALWAYS check the tail: image_end = e_shoff+e_shnum*e_shentsize (PE: pefile overlay start); len > image_end => OVERLAY with a\n  day magic (PK19 D19, RS20 D20; D27 = bare RAW HCFG, no magic, \"scan backward from the end\" = rfind loop until crc-valid):\n  o = data.rfind(magic); parse EVERY header field the QUESTION lists (size ids = that field,\n  hcfg_resource_size = u32@8), verify bounds/sha256, run its transform, HCFG at the stated offset; overlay_size = len-o.\n  NOT FOUND => hidden elsewhere: (1) packed? unpack; (2) AES S-box 637c777b / TEA 9e3779b9 / 'expand 32-byte k' => find key+IV\n  near the call, decrypt with pycryptodome; (3) runs of mov [rbp-x], imm => stack-built: collect imms with capstone or\n  emulate the builder with unicorn; (4) PE .rsrc / .NET resource / jar non-class entry / gaps between sections (slack) /\n  custom ELF notes (`readelf -nW`) / compressed `C`-flag sections (`readelf -zx`) / archive appended after the image;\n  (5) .init_array / TLS callback decoder => emulate it. Offsets: raw=the H, base64=the S (GM-confirmed); else first stored byte.\nFIELDS: format = container only (elf/pe/macho?/jar; .NET pe_cli) | machine/architecture = container machine word |\n  qualifier ids dNN_analysis_<tag>_<field> -> member whose file name has <tag> (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/\n  plugin, vulnerable/corrected, D27 gcc/tcc; LONGEST member-name token); THEN the member the QUESTION names; \"decode both role\n  members, require equal\" (D24/D25/D27) => decode all, assert equal, use the common value; sha256_K = zip order | config_* verbatim |\n  has_<x>_section = literal section name | hex fields lowercase 0x | never chase the prompt's theme: answer only asked ids.\n  New-language member = carried-over header ids (post first); twist = the NEW field family: its longest question is the\n  spec (rules, offsets, transforms, hashes). `none` only for ABSENT things.\nCRASH (D26, ASKED): sidecar {\"schema\":\"huntress.synthetic_crash.v1\",\"kind\":<Exception>,\"frames\":[innermost..outermost]};\n  fault method = frames[0] verbatim; \"frames match methods\" = every frame in the primary class's method_info names -> true/false.\n  Native sequel: core `readelf -nW` NT_PRSTATUS RIP / MDMP ExceptionStream -> `addr2line -f -e bin`, capstone it. Never run it.\nATTRIBUTION (D27 theme, UNASKED; roles = compiler names): gcc = DW_AT_producer `GNU C99 <ver> <flags>` (`readelf --debug-dump=\n  info F|grep -m2 producer`), `.lto_priv/.constprop/.isra` syms, FILE crtstuff.c, DWARF; tcc = `.stab`/`.stabstr`, `tcc_backtrace`,\n  `.hash` only, unmerged `.text.<x>`/`.rodata.str1.1`, 1 GNU_PROPERTY note per object; libc = PT_INTERP; `.comment` may be ABSENT.\nTHEME FACTS (unasked): dynamic_trace.v1 template (family `<lang>_<theme>_trace` names the theme), env HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL\n  (+TRIGGER_FAULT); D21 NEEDED/exports; D22 ImplMap; D23 predicates; D24 `score` null->NPE; D25 `parse-frame` (nth v 4)->IOOBE.\nBACKFILL ids on OLD groups (D8, D17): marker, recover_code (decimal), mangled_score/typeinfo_symbol (bare _ZNK/_ZTI; PE .text$),\n  has_* true/false, methods (JSON incl <init>), access_flags (decimal), method_count (ALL method_info). Derive from bytes.\nhcfg_storage (enum): base64 carrier -> base64 | literal HCFG in section `.hcfg` -> raw_hcfg_section | in WASM data seg ->\n  wasm_data_segment | in another native data section (.data/.rodata) -> raw_const_array | else raw. Stripped d01 => recover_code none.\nUNGUESSABLE label: <=10 probes, HELP.md, re-pull contract. MASTERY: cache per (delivery, member)/sha256, never id(bytes).\nFORWARD HINTS: grep each contract for tokens/days not today's (open: enum `neko_bytecode`). Values re-shaped in TT/M: copy verbatim.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n```json\n[\n  {\"id\": \"crash-sidecar-generic-parser\", \"concept\": \"Crash/trace SIDECAR anywhere in a member (D26 shape generalised): locate a crash record in a jar/zip entry, ELF section or note, PE RCDATA/.NET resource, overlay or a separate `dNN--*.json`/`.txt` member, and expose its facts\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 asked crash_fault_method (= frames[0] verbatim) and crash_frames_match_methods (every frame in the primary classfile method-name set) from `crash/trace.json` = {schema: huntress.synthetic_crash.v1, kind, frames[innermost..]} inside challenges/day26/binary-crash-course/single_solve/work/extracted/evidence/d26--sample.jar. Build lib.binary.crash_sidecar(member_bytes) -> {schema, kind, frames, frame_count, fault_method, outer_method, raw}: search zip entries whose name ends trace.json/crash*.json/*.trace, any JSON object with a `frames`/`stack`/`backtrace` list in raw bytes (ELF section, PE resource, overlay, UTF-16 too), and text traces. Normalise frame strings in every likely shape: bare `stageThree`, `Class.method`, `pkg.Class.method(File.groovy:12)`, `module!func+0x1a`, `func+0x1a/0x40`, `#0 0x... in func file:line`, raw `0x401136` (-> resolve via symtab). Predicates: frames subset of method set (JVM method_info names, .NET MethodDef names, ELF/PE FUNC symbols), frame[0] defined in the primary unit, frames form a valid static call chain (see jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts). Missing sidecar -> `none`/`false`. Fixtures: the D26 jar + synthesised variants (renamed entry path, frames with descriptors, sidecar in an ELF section).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"jvm-call-chain-throw-site-facts\", \"concept\": \"Static call chain + throw sites for a JVM primary class (what a stack trace should look like): per method its callees and the exceptions it throws, so a reported trace can be verified or derived\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D26 (unasked): Day26Variant000 main -> stageOne -> stageTwo -> stageThree (invokestatic), stageThree = `new java/lang/IllegalStateException` ... `athrow`; main compares HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT via ScriptBytecodeAdapter.compareEqual and catches the exception (trace effects bounded_caught_exception_only). Build from Code attributes: callees per method (invokestatic/virtual/special/interface; invokedynamic bootstrap names; Groovy dynamic call sites = the `$createCallSiteArray_1` string array when the class is not @CompileStatic), thrown classes (`new X` ... `athrow`, `athrow` of a param), exception_table (handler ranges + catch types), LineNumberTable lines per throw, `throws` (Exceptions attribute). Answers: fault_method from bytecode alone (the only method that athrows the trace kind), call depth, caller of X, catch site, line of the throw, `frames_are_call_chain` predicate. Same for Kotlin/Scala ($ module) /Clojure (invokeStatic) layouts; fixtures: D24/D25/D26 jars.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"elf-core-dump-triage\", \"concept\": \"Native crash dump: ELF core file (ET_CORE) as a group member beside its executable -- signal, faulting RIP, registers, mapped files, fault address\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Natural native sequel to D26 ('the dump is a confession ... find the faulting instruction'). Parse PT_NOTE (owner CORE/LINUX): NT_PRSTATUS (pr_cursig, pr_pid, user_regs_struct order r15..rip,cs,eflags,rsp,ss,fs_base..), NT_PRPSINFO (pr_fname, pr_psargs), NT_SIGINFO (si_signo, si_errno, si_code SEGV_MAPERR=1/ACCERR=2, si_addr), NT_AUXV (AT_ENTRY, AT_PHDR, AT_EXECFN), NT_FILE (count, page_size, start/end/file_ofs + names), NT_FPREGSET; PT_LOAD memory for stack reads. Map RIP to (module, file offset) via NT_FILE and to a function via the companion member's symtab/.eh_frame (build-id NT_GNU_BUILD_ID match). Labels: signal names `SIGSEGV`/`SIGABRT`/`SIGFPE`/`SIGILL`/`SIGBUS`/`SIGTRAP` and numbers 11/6/8/4/7/5; hex with 0x. Fixtures: compile tiny C crashers (null write, div0, abort via __stack_chk_fail, ud2) and make cores with `gdb -batch -ex run -ex generate-core-file` on OUR fixtures only (never run a challenge sample); 32-bit + AArch64 cores via synthetic note writers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"faulting-instruction-locator\", \"concept\": \"'Find the faulting instruction': map a fault pc/offset (from a core, minidump, text report or the question) to its function and decode/classify the instruction\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Inputs: VA or file offset + member. Containing function via .symtab/.dynsym FUNC ranges, then .eh_frame FDE ranges (stripped), PE .pdata RUNTIME_FUNCTION, Mach-O LC_FUNCTION_STARTS; JVM: bytecode offset -> method via Code ranges + LineNumberTable. Decode with capstone intel in the GM convention (lowercase, decimal immediates, no trailing space: `mov dword ptr [rax], 0`), plus facts: mnemonic, memory operand base/index/disp, access size, read vs write, offset within function (`func+0x1a`). Classify: null-pointer read/write (base reg 0 / si_addr < 0x1000), divide error (`div`/`idiv`, SIGFPE), `ud2`/`int3`/`hlt` trap, call through bad pointer, stack-protector abort (`call __stack_chk_fail`), assert/abort. Fixtures from the elf-core-dump-triage crashers (x86-64, i386, AArch64).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bug-reachability-gating-facts\", \"concept\": \"'Trace its reachability': the call path from the entry point to the vulnerable call and the input/env predicates that must hold (env var names + compared values, argv/stdin/file checks), per member and per host model\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 (unasked): Clojure `-main` -> System.getenv(HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL) compared to `workstation`, getenv(HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT) Util.equiv \\\"1\\\" -> chooses frame const__3 [1 2] (2 elements) vs const__7 [1 2 3 4 5] -> parse-frame (nth 4). Build lib.binary.reachability_facts(member, target_fn): JVM -- walk invokeStatic/IFn.invoke edges from main/-main (resolve Var.getRawRoot of `RT.var` names to fn classes), collect the getenv/equals/equiv/lookupswitch predicates on the path and the constant collections (Tuple.create arity / array sizes) fed to the target; native -- capstone call graph (prebuilt callgraph-indirect-flow-facts) + getenv/strcmp/argv compares before the call. Output: call_path (JSON names), gate_env_vars (JSON, order of use), gate_values, trigger_condition text, reachable_for_<host_model> booleans, input_size_on_trigger (2) vs safe (5). Fixtures: D25 jars + D24 jars + a C twin with getenv-gated memcpy.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"crash-exploitability-facts\", \"concept\": \"Native 'prove it is broken' facts: stack buffer size, distance from buffer to saved RIP/canary, overflow length that faults, faulting instruction, mitigations (canary/NX/PIE/RELRO)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"From capstone over the vulnerable function: frame size (`sub rsp, N`), buffer offset (`lea rdi, [rbp-0xNN]` passed to gets/strcpy/read/memcpy/scanf %s), canary load `mov rax, fs:0x28` + `__stack_chk_fail`, read length argument; distance_to_return = NN + 8 (rbp) ; first faulting length via unicorn emulation with a cyclic (de Bruijn) pattern; checksec-style facts from program headers (GNU_STACK flags, GNU_RELRO + BIND_NOW, ET_DYN+INTERP). Corrected twin: same facts showing the bound. Fixtures: gcc -fno-stack-protector / -fstack-protector-strong pairs.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"symbolic-input-solver\", \"concept\": \"Find an input that reaches a target (vulnerable path, accept branch, decoy vs success) with angr/z3 when hand-evaluation is impractical: crackme/license checks, multi-step guards\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"angr (venv) blank_state at the function with symbolic args/stdin, avoid-list = failure branches, find = target address (crash site, success string xref, `return 1`); z3 directly for JVM/IL guard chains extracted by the bytecode evaluators (hashCode lookupswitch -> string preimage among the binary's own literals first). Hard caps: 60 s, 4 GB; output the concrete input as hex + printable. Fixtures: gcc serial-check (per-char xor/add compare), a hash-gated branch, and the D24 host-model lookupswitch (preimages analysis/workstation/sandbox). D25 'trace its reachability' = which env values reach the bug: include the D25 Clojure `-main` (HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL / HUNTRESS_TRIGGER_FAULT compares) as a fixture.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"member-basename-vocabulary\", \"concept\": \"Member basenames re-labelled between days (D22: `dNN--variant-000.*` -> `dNN--sample.*`, `sample-stripped`, `sample-plugin`) and questions reworded to match; D23 timed modes re-shaped the VALUES too (campaign `BRNN-<8 uppercase hex>`, d01 marker `BR01-<8hex>`, FILE symbol `sample.c`)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Group members by the `dNN--` prefix only; derive role/tag from the token after the stem (stripped/symbolized, compact/direct, loader/plugin) or from the extension; never require `variant-` or `sample`. A regression case with renamed members (sed the names in a copy of the zip listing) keeps the router honest. D23: never regex-validate a value shape (`BRNN-\\\\d{3}`) or derive anything from the `00V` index; copy decoded values verbatim. D24 timed modes re-shaped domain (`<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid`), mutex (`Global\\\\Huntress<12 uppercase hex>`) and url (`https://<word>-<8hex>.dayNN.example.invalid/<word>/<10hex>`) too; role tokens `vulnerable`/`corrected` follow `sample-`. D25 timed modes added domain/url words edge/cache/vault/proxy/node and path words vault/edge/stage/sync/gate; url host word independent of the domain word.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-revision-watch\", \"concept\": \"Organizers revise the live contract mid-day (D17: exact_text -> enum + rule text)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"When an exact_text label resists ~10 probes: write HELP, then re-pull the contract (`hctf status <id>`) every ~20-30 min and diff question text/answer_format per id; D17 the revision converted ~3.5 h and ~10.9k rejected probes into CORRECT within a minute. Never run mass automated label grouptests on a closed-vocabulary GM field.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"contract-forward-hints\", \"concept\": \"The live contract leaks upcoming days: tokens and day numbers that do not belong to today\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D19 leaked D20's overlay magic ('PK19 for Day 19 or RS20 for Day 20') and it came true. Still open after D21 (D20/D21 contracts added no new token; carried-over questions byte-identical): the format enum lists `neko_bytecode` (unseen), and d07_analysis_method_count says 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit'. Each day, grep the contract for magic-like tokens (`[A-Z]{2}\\\\d{2}`), enum values never confirmed, and 'Day NN' > today; record them in solver/NOTES.md and the coverage atlas so the prebuild targets them. The solver maps a `<2 caps><NN>` magic to the group whose day is NN. D22: no new token/day; all members silently renamed dNN--variant-000.* -> dNN--sample.* and the d03 questions dropped 'variant-' -- solvers must not key on 'variant-'. D23: no new token/day either (Day 26 and neko_bytecode still open). D24: no new token/day; EVERY question reworded into a spec (sha256 'ZIP central-directory order (1-based)', format rule list, full HCFG layout + per-container carrier rule) -- Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open; D24 Scala's `Foo$` module vs forwarder Main-Class is a plausible meaning of 'primary classfile named by that unit'. D25: no new token/day; d25 ids copy the D24 wording verbatim; Day 26 + neko_bytecode still open (Clojure's `__init` vs gen-class stub is a 2nd example of 'primary classfile named by that unit'). D26: the d07 'for Day 26 use the primary classfile named by that unit' leak came TRUE (Groovy jar; the primary classfile = the manifest Main-Class `Day26Variant000`, not the `$_main_closure1` closure). Only `neko_bytecode` remains open; D26 contract added no new token/day.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"neko-bytecode-member\", \"concept\": \"Neko VM bytecode member (`.n`, magic NEKO): container parse, globals/strings, HCFG location, labels for format/architecture/machine\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"The GM's own format enum (d12-d19 since D19) lists `neko_bytecode` = a Neko member is scheduled. `apt install neko haxe` (candidates neko 2.4.1, haxe 4.3.7) then build fixtures: a Haxe `-neko out.n` program and a raw `nekoc` program holding the HCFG as a string literal (raw bytes and base64 'SENGR...') -- plus `nekotools boot` (Neko standalone ELF = neko VM + appended bytecode, another overlay!). Parser: 'NEKO' u32 nglobals, u32 nfields, u32 codesize; globals (type byte: 1 var, 2 function, 3 string u16/u32 len, 4 float, 5 debug, 6 version), fields (NUL-terminated names), code. Facts: format `neko_bytecode`, globals_count, fields list, string globals, hcfg offset (start of the string payload = the `H`/`S`), has_neko_runtime; architecture/machine for a VM are UNKNOWN -- record candidates (`neko`, `nekovm`, `none`) and read the question text first. Ensure lib.binary magic dispatch and the solver's format() return `neko_bytecode` for raw .n and recognise a nekotools-booted ELF (format elf + overlay).\"},","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hkkfos1p4M7oGABxTQ1q73","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
